Subject: tray: load icon from installed PNG so DMS gets an IconPixmap

DMS (Dux Modular Shell) fails to resolve the SystemTrayIcon theme name
("WARN quickshell.service.sni.item: Unable to create pixmap for tray
icon") even though the icon exists in /usr/local/share/icons/hicolor
(with index.theme) and ~/.local/share/icons/hicolor. It renders items
that provide IconPixmap (e.g. Joplin) or a file-path IconName (e.g.
ProtonVPN) fine.

Setting icon.source to a bare absolute SVG path exported an EMPTY
IconPixmap array (no image-load logs at all — the QML icon loader did
not pick it up). Using an explicit file:// URL to a pre-rendered PNG
makes Qt export a real IconPixmap, which DMS renders.

PNGs are 48x48 renders of the symbolic SVGs (white on transparent,
matching the dark DMS tray); they must be installed alongside this
patch (see update.sh / installed-files.txt).

AI-generated local patch, 2026-11-25 (Claude Code). Drop when DMS gains
proper theme-name resolution or the distro package works under DMS.

--- a/src/contents/ui/TrayIcon.qml
+++ b/src/contents/ui/TrayIcon.qml
@@ -30,9 +30,13 @@
     property Main mainWindow: null

     readonly property string iconName: DbMain.bypass ? applicationId + "-off-symbolic" : applicationId + "-symbolic"

+    // Local patch (2026-11-25): DMS cannot resolve the theme name above,
+    // so load the installed PNG directly; Qt then exports an IconPixmap.
+    readonly property string iconSource: "file:///usr/local/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/" + iconName + ".png"
+
     visible: DbMain.showTrayIcon && canUseSysTray
-    icon.name: iconName
+    icon.source: iconSource
     tooltip: applicationName

     onActivated: {
